    "scenario": "IP Overlay DMVPN Phase 2 Spoke to Spoke",
    "goals": "• {{router4_name}} is the transit provider. The hub {{router1_name}} and the two spokes {{router2_name}} and {{router3_name}} each have one public link to it and a default route towards it, and each has a private network on Loopback1:\n    hub {{router1_name}}: public {{link1_ip1}}, private {{router1_loopback1_cidr}}\n    spoke {{router2_name}}: public {{link2_ip1}}, private {{router2_loopback1_cidr}}\n    spoke {{router3_name}}: public {{link3_ip1}}, private {{router3_loopback1_cidr}}\n• {{router4_name}} only knows its three directly connected public subnets and must never learn the private networks.\n• A hub and spoke dynamic multipoint VPN is already running on the NBMA subnet {{nbma_cidr}} over Tunnel{{tunnel_id}}, with tunnel key and NHRP network identifier {{nhrp_network_id}} and NHRP authentication {{nhrp_auth}}. EIGRP AS {{eigrp_asn}} carries all three private networks over the overlay.\n    hub {{router1_name}}: {{nbma_ip1}}, multipoint GRE, accepts dynamic registrations\n    spokes {{router2_name}} ({{nbma_ip2}}) and {{router3_name}} ({{nbma_ip3}}): point to point GRE aimed at the hub\n• Every packet between the two spokes is therefore hairpinned through {{router1_name}}. Convert the overlay so the spokes can build a direct tunnel to each other on demand.\n• On both spokes, replace the fixed point to point tunnel with a multipoint GRE tunnel that keeps registering with the hub as its next hop server. Because a multipoint tunnel no longer has a fixed destination, the hub tunnel address {{nbma_ip1}} must be statically mapped to the hub public address {{link1_ip1}}, and multicast traffic must still be mapped to {{link1_ip1}} so the EIGRP hellos keep working.\n• On the hub, stop replacing the next hop in the EIGRP updates it relays between the spokes, so each spoke learns the other spoke's private network with the other spoke's tunnel address as next hop instead of {{nbma_ip1}}.\n• Do not change the tunnel addresses, the tunnel key, the NHRP network identifier, the NHRP authentication or the EIGRP AS number.\n• Result: {{router2_name}} must reach {{router3_loopback1_cidr}} with next hop {{nbma_ip3}}, {{router3_name}} must reach {{router2_loopback1_cidr}} with next hop {{nbma_ip2}}, and the two private networks must still be able to ping each other.",
